MAMBA-NIKE — NGCC API_PKC KEX Package
======================================

This directory contains the five submitted MAMBA-NIKE KEX instances,
their Reference and x86-64 Optimized implementations, canonical KATs,
and API conformance tests.

Algorithm Summary
-----------------
  Type:           responder-static one-pass KEX
  Ring:           Z_q[x]/(x^n + 1)
  Modulus:        q = 2^13 = 8192
  Reconciliation: NewHope-style D4 helper data
  KDF:            SHAKE256("MAMBA-NIKE-KDF20" || nu || pk_B || M1)

Multiplication Backends
-----------------------
  Reference:
    portable coefficient-domain Toom-Cook-4 negacyclic convolution.

  Optimized AVX2:
    fixed-loop direct negacyclic accumulation in 16-bit AVX2 lanes via
    poly_mul_small().  The final q-1 mask is exact after modulo-2^16 lane
    wraparound because q divides 2^16.  The implementation never skips
    zero secret coefficients.  Non-AVX2 builds use the Toom-Cook fallback.

Submitted Instances
-------------------
  Instance          n     eta   t_pk  t_u  pk     sk_api  M1    ss   KAT suffix
  MAMBA-NIKE-128   1024     2      9   10  1184   3232   1568   32   2752
  MAMBA-NIKE-192   1024     3     10   10  1312   3360   1568   32   2880
  MAMBA-NIKE-256   1024     7     10   10  1312   3360   1568   32   2880
  MAMBA-NIKE-384   2048     2     11   11  2848   6944   3360   48   6208
  MAMBA-NIKE-512   2048     5     11   11  2848   6944   3360   64   6208

The values above document the already frozen profile headers.  The current
optimization does not modify parameters.json or any params.h file.

Directory Layout
----------------
  Implementations/
    Reference_Implementation/MAMBA-NIKE-{128,192,256,384,512}/
    Optimized_Implementation/MAMBA-NIKE-{128,192,256,384,512}/
  KAT/MAMBA-NIKE-*/PQCkexKAT_*.{req,rsp}
  Test_Vectors/KAT_KEX_MAMBA-NIKE-*.txt
  Internal_Tests/NGCC_API/api_check.c

KAT Generation
--------------
  bash generate_all_kats.sh

Reference is the canonical KAT source.  Optimized builds must match the
corresponding Reference raw KAT file byte for byte.
